  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Neuronetics’ core U.S. clinic business is gaining momentum, buoyed by strong SPRAVATO (esketamine) adoption and firm pricing, while NeuroStar system shipments are rising. Treatment session revenue faced headwinds from customer inventory destocking, though underlying system utilization improved. The growth narrative is anchored in expanding neurohealth therapy demand, with SPRAVATO acting as a complementary tailwind that reinforces the device ecosystem. No macro or regulatory drags surfaced in the commentary.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** New CEO Dan Reuvers has begun a listening tour and is actively evaluating the go-to-market model, clinic execution, and overall business structure. Concurrently, an activist shareholder holding a significant stake is publicly agitating for strategic alternatives, including a potential sale of the TMS business, and cites substantial upside from current levels. Management reaffirmed its full-year outlook, projecting confidence amid the leadership transition and activist pressure, placing the company squarely in a narrative of potential strategic evolution and value unlocking.",
